  ["ac_scenemodel_001", "Chapter 1 · Continuation and drafts"],
  ["ac_scenemodel_002", "Continuation transfers current business state to another device. Business data, the system quick result and window loading are separate facts and must be observed separately."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_003", "Selection and unsaved changes are part of the context alongside note text. Successful transfer does not mean the user has agreed to overwrite a local draft."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_004", "Reading progress consists of the book version, chapter and paragraph anchor. This book is bundled with the app; only progress, not the book file, is transferred."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_005", "Chapter 2 · Versions and conflicts"],
  ["ac_scenemodel_006", "Document identity determines what a revision number means. Revisions of different documents cannot be merged by taking the maximum."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_007", "If local content is unsaved, let the user accept the incoming version or keep local content. A higher remote revision must not silently replace it."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_008", "Persist before replacing the page. Restore the old value after a failed write; if rollback cannot be confirmed, freeze further writes to avoid increasing uncertainty."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_009", "Chapter 3 · Continue working"],
  ["ac_scenemodel_010", "After restoration, the recipient can edit, add bookmarks, change chapters and initiate continuation again through the system entry."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_011", "A loaded page only proves its container is ready, not that the text selection or reading anchor is positioned. The actual business page must report positioning."],
  ["ac_scenemodel_012", "Controlled host tests check business rules; SDK builds check static contracts. Real cross-device behavior still requires authorized verification through the system entry."],
